.TH "JT-DECODED" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
jt-decoded \- record timed audio segments and invoke weak-signal decoders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jt-decoded
.RI "[-w | -8 | -4] [-d directory] [-x decoder] [-o source] [-L locale] [-k] [-v] [-V] destination"
.SH STATUS
.B Deprecated
Use
.BR pcmrecord (1)
instead.
.SH DESCRIPTION
jt-decoded receives RTP PCM sessions, writes cycle-aligned WAVE files, and
invokes an external WSPR, FT8, or FT4 decoder on completed files. Decoder
output is directed to standard output. Decoder executables are separate
software and must be installed. This older combined recorder/decoder is
distinct from the separate pcmrecord and decode-service pipelines described in
the project FT8 documentation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-w"
Select WSPR: 120-second cycle, wsprd decoder. This is the default.
.TP
.B "\-8"
Select FT8: 15-second cycle, decode_ft8 decoder.
.TP
.B "\-4"
Select FT4: 7.5-second cycle, decode_ft8 decoder in FT4 mode.
.TP
.B "\-d directory"
Set recording/work directory. Default current directory. It must be accessible
and writable.
.TP
.B "\-x pathname"
Override the decoder executable for FT8 and FT4. Does not override the WSPR
decoder.
.TP
.B "\-o source"
Restrict reception to one network source.
.TP
.B "\-L locale"
Set locale; initially taken from LANG.
.TP
.B "\-k"
Keep temporary WAVE files after decoding.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Increase diagnostics.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH INPUT
The legacy path handles 16-bit PCM using its RTP payload mappings. Use a
compatible mono PCM stream, not Opus or floating-point samples. Verify decoder
sample-rate requirements. It derives the decoder base frequency from SSRC,
assuming the SSRC represents frequency in Hz; arbitrary SSRC assignments can
therefore produce incorrect reported frequencies. Cycle completion depends on
subsequent packet arrival; a stopped stream can leave its last partial file
unprocessed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Decode FT8 using a selected audio group and writable work directory:
.PP
.nf
jt\-decoded \-8 \-d /var/tmp/ft8\-work ft8\-pcm.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
pcmrecord(1), wd-record(1), radiod(8)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
